### Imputation Diagnostics

Good imputation practice requires checking that imputed values are plausible. Honaker
and King (2010) suggest two primary diagnostics.

#### Density overlap

Imputed values (red) should be broadly consistent with observed values (black): the
same support and rough shape. Systematic divergence suggests model misspecification.

::: {.panel-tabset}

