### Option B: Mundlak Device (Recommended)

The Mundlak (1978) device adds the **within-unit means** of all time-varying regressors
to the RE specification. The RE–FE choice becomes a test of whether these group means
are jointly zero — a linear restriction that pools straightforwardly under Rubin's rules.
The joint test is implemented below using the **D2 statistic** of Li, Meng, Raghunathan
& Rubin (1991), which combines the $M$ per-imputation Wald chi-squared statistics into a
single $F$ reference distribution rather than simply averaging them.

::: {.panel-tabset}

#### R


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Compute group means in each imputed dataset and add to the data
add_group_means <- function(d) {
  d |>
    group_by(country) |>
    mutate(
      m_polity = mean(polity,    na.rm = TRUE),
      m_lpop   = mean(log(pop),  na.rm = TRUE),
      m_lgdppc = mean(log(gdp.pc), na.rm = TRUE)
    ) |>
    ungroup()
}

a_mundlak <- a.out
a_mundlak$imputations <- lapply(a.out$imputations, add_group_means)

mundlak_formula <- tariff ~ polity + log(pop) + log(gdp.pc) +
                             m_polity + m_lpop + m_lgdppc

res_mundlak <- pool_plm(
  amelia_out = a_mundlak,
  formula    = mundlak_formula,
  index      = c("country", "year"),
  model      = "random"
)

# The group-mean terms test RE consistency
res_mundlak |>
  select(term, estimate, std.error, statistic, df, p.value) |>
  mutate(role = if_else(str_starts(term, "m_"), "Mundlak term", "Structural")) |>
  gt(groupname_col = "role") |>
  tab_header(
    title    = "Mundlak (1978) RE model — MI Pooled",
    subtitle = "H₀: group-mean coefficients = 0 ↔ RE is consistent"
  ) |>
  fmt_number(columns = c(estimate, std.error, statistic, p.value), decimals = 4) |>
  fmt_number(columns = df, decimals = 1) |>
  tab_style(
    style     = cell_fill(color = "#fef9c3"),
    locations = cells_body(rows = p.value < 0.05)
  )
```

